    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate today's edition of **The Sabudh Dispatch** newspaper.\n\nUse the workflow context below.\n\nSubscriber: {{ $json.subscriberName }}\n\nTopics to cover:\n{{ $json.topics }}\n\nSpecial interests:\n{{ $json.customInterests }}\n\nDate:\n{{ $json.todayDate }}\n\nCreate a professional newspaper front page with:\n\n• A main headline\n• A subheadline\n• News sections based on the topics\n• 2–3 articles per section\n\nReturn STRICT JSON.\n",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are the editor of a digital newspaper called **The Sabudh Dispatch**.\n\nYour job is to generate the **content for a newspaper front page**.\n\nYou MUST rely entirely on the context fields provided by the workflow.\n\nContext fields provided by the system:\n\nSubscriber Name: {{ $json.subscriberName }}\nTopics: {{ $json.topics }}\nCustom Interests: {{ $json.customInterests }}\nDate: {{ $json.todayDate }}\n\nRules:\n\n1. Only generate news sections based on the provided topics.\n2. If custom interests exist, create an additional section called \"Special Interest\".\n3. Use a professional newspaper tone similar to Financial Times or The Economist.\n4. Headlines should be concise and journalistic.\n5. Each section should contain 2–4 short articles.\n6. Each article summary must be 1–2 sentences.\n\nReturn STRICT JSON with this schema:\n\n{\n\"masthead\": \"The Sabudh Dispatch\",\n\"date\": \"date from context\",\n\"headline\": \"Main front page headline\",\n\"subheadline\": \"Supporting headline\",\n\"sections\": [\n{\n\"title\": \"Section name\",\n\"articles\": [\n{\n\"title\": \"Article headline\",\n\"summary\": \"Short summary\"\n}\n]\n}\n]\n}\n\nReturn only JSON.\n"
        }
      },
      "id": "60490f6a-c7dd-4b2c-8e9c-b82a30202a6a",
      "name": "AI Agent - Fetch News",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 1.6,
      "position": [
        1248,
        160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const ctx = $('Set Subscriber Context').first().json;\nconst name = ctx.subscriberName || 'Subscriber';\nconst email = ctx.subscriberEmail;\nconst todayDate = ctx.todayDate;\nconst newspaperHtml = $('Code in JavaScript').first().json.html;\n\nconst html = `\n<div style=\"font-family: Georgia, serif; max-width: 700px; margin: auto; background: #fff; padding: 30px;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; border-bottom: 3px solid #222; padding-bottom: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n    <h1 style=\"font-size: 36px; margin: 0; letter-spacing: 2px;\">The Sabudh Dispatch</h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #666; margin-top: 4px;\">${todayDate}</p>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"font-size: 15px; color: #333;\">Good morning <strong>${name}</strong>, here is your personalized daily briefing.</p>\n  ${newspaperHtml}\n  <hr style=\"margin-top: 30px; border: none; border-top: 2px solid #222;\">\n  <p style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #999; text-align: center;\">You received this because you subscribed to The Sabudh Dispatch.<br>Powered by n8n Automation &middot; Hotbot Studios</p>\n</div>\n`;\n\nreturn [{ json: { subscriberEmail: email, emailHtml: html, todayDate: todayDate } }];"
      },
      "id": "a32c60fd-4994-4475-a1e4-17a6e0a985e8",
      "name": "Format Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
